==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|mallarky}}
* {{l|en|malarky}}
* {{l|en|mullarkey}}

Malarkey could have originated from the Greek slang words malaka (used to describe a stupid person) or malakies (used to describe  stupid words, actions, and/or beliefs). Both of which were derived from the Greek word malakia. The literal meaning of which is the act of masturbation. There is some preliminary evidence corraberating the "Greek origin theory" (the word seems to have originated in the united states sometime in the early 1900's in the Midwest, a place there were many Greeks working in the steel mills). However,  further research is needed for a definitive answer. As there are other theories of an Irish origin of the word.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/məˈlɑɹ.ki/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɑː(ɹ)ki|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# [[nonsense|Nonsense]]; [[rubbish]].
#: ''I decided it was a bunch of '''malarkey''' and stopped reading about halfway through.

